  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure across the area, will provide mainly dry conditions to \nthe region, however, isolated to scattered showers and storms are \npossible through mid week, as multiple weak shortwaves cross the \narea. Chances are low enough that it was not included in the \nforecast per the blend of models for most days this week. \n\nThe main story during the period concerns increasing heat and \nhumidity as we progress into next week as upper ridge builds across \nthe area. Temperatures next week will climb into the 90s for much of \nthe lower elevations, and this combined with increasing humidity \nwill result in heat indices in the upper 90s to lower 100s at times. \nHeat headlines may be needed for a period next week.\n\nRidge breaks down towards the end of the work week, with increasing \nchances for showers and storms, and a break in the oppressive\nheat.",
